  "$schema": "https://o2csi.github.io/candeo/device-definition.schema.json",
  "name": "Razer DeathStalker V2 Pro",
  "notes": [
    "Survey: docs/protocol/deathstalker-v2-pro.md.",
    "A 90-byte feature report behind report id 0: status, transaction 9f, the argument length at 5, class and command at 6 and 7, the arguments from 8, and the XOR of bytes 2 to 87 in 88.",
    "A frame is the six rows, 22 cells each, lit or not: sending only the 106 keys leaves the last rows frozen (section 6). Then the custom effect, which is what hands the lights to the host.",
    "Status 02 validates the class and the command, never an argument's value (section 8).",
    "Static and Breathing take a colour the survey never found in a read-back, so they are not offered; the wave's two values are the only ones captured."
  ],
  "match": { "vid": "1532", "pid": "0292", "interface": 3 },
  "surveyed": "1.5",
  "inspect": "razer",
  "report": {
    "wire": "feature",
    "length": 90,
    "prefix": "00",
    "checksum": { "function": "xor", "from": 2, "to": 87, "at": 88 },
    "command": { "class": 6, "id": 7 }
  },
  "frame": {
    "each": {
      "by": "row",
      "send": ["00 9f 00 00 00 {length:8} 0f 03 00 00 {row} {start} {end} {lights}"],
      "light": "{r} {g} {b}"
    },
    "close": ["00 9f 00 00 00 06 0f 02 00 00 08 00 00 00"]
  },
  "brightness": ["00 9f 00 00 00 03 0f 04 00 00 {level}"],
  "firmware": {
    "send": "00 9f 00 00 00 06 0f 02 00 00 {kind} 00 00 00",
    "off": "00",
    "effects": [
      { "id": "hardware:spectrumCycle", "kind": "03", "name": "hues cycling over the whole keyboard" },
      { "id": "hardware:wave", "kind": "04", "send": "00 9f 00 00 00 06 0f 02 00 00 04 02 28 00", "name": "a wave, in the one direction and speed captured" }
    ]
  },
